# ELB-KX-001: Load balancer listener does not offer hybrid post-quantum key exchange
# Resource: aws_lb_listener.defaulted
# Safety: auto
# Note: Same protocols and ciphers as the current policy, plus TLS 1.3 and hybrid post-quantum key exchange: no client loses a protocol version or a cipher suite. The hybrid key share makes handshake messages larger, and the AWS KMS post-quantum TLS page warns that legacy proxies or firewalls with deep packet inspection might block them, so watch the connection logs after the change. It keeps the TLS 1.0 and 1.1 the current policy admits; AWS recommends ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-Res-PQ-2025-09 once the connection logs show no TLS 1.0 or 1.1 clients. Clients that cannot negotiate ML-KEM keep working on these policies; only the key exchange changes for clients that can. Check the connection logs' key exchange field after the change.
# EdgePQ does not apply patches. Review, then apply with: git apply <file>, then run terraform fmt (an inserted line may re-align its neighbours)
--- a/fail.tf
+++ b/fail.tf
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
   port              = 8443
   protocol          = "HTTPS"
   certificate_arn   = var.cert
+  ssl_policy        = "ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-0-PQ-2025-09"
   default_action {
     type             = "forward"
     target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.tg.arn
